{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices","id":976176,"title":"Using automatic successes replacing exploding dices?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-25T17:08:22-07:00","id":976176,"title":"Using automatic successes replacing exploding dices?","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> Im running a werewolf game and my players arent happy with how the exploding dice mechanic works.<br /> <br /> More often than not the pcs would get a 10, get happy with a reroll and then get dissapointed when it doesnt reach success.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the spectrum so far 3 games in i have had many situations when a goon with 4 dices keep exploding dices 2 or 3 times until a pc died (i let them burn a WP to survive)<br /> <br /> The group comes from playing OWoD 20 in which a 10 again was replaced with an automatic success (meaning if you roll a 10 it counted as 2 successes instead of 1) and one of the player suggested me that house rule.<br /> <br /> While owod and cod are very similar they still got differences. Has anyone try this? Or see a huge problem i am not seeing?<br /> <br /> The idea would be that any ability that allows for exploding dice like 8-again, 9-again or 10-again would be replace with counting as 2 success trading the posibility of &quot;infinity rerolls&quot; for 2 sure successes when triggered. This would not apply to rote action rerolls.<br /> <br /> Thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:36:33-07:00","id":976188,"title":"","content":"It would make combat deadlier.<br /> <br /> In your examples, for instance. Your group gets a 10, and gets an extra success. But a goon with 4 dices gets 2 10s, getting 4 successes. Add Weapon Bonus on top of that.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind probability is the same for NPCs and PCs, you should probably avoid using groups of NPCs as antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-25-2016, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:08:09-07:00","id":976246,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't hugely alter things. You would see more successes on average, and more exceptional successes, but it wouldn't impact the pass/fail nature of basic rolls, and if both parties benefit from the rule it shouldn't change contested rolls. It does make getting an exceptional on two dice literally impossible, where before it was just extremely unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:32:00-07:00","id":976264,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think it would change most things prominently, but it could affect combat.<br /> <br /> It does increase your chances of a dramatic success, but since you need five successes for that, it's not going to unbalance things too much.<br /> <br /> As nofather said, combat is the real point of contention. CoD combat is pretty damn deadly (particularly after the 2E rules changes), and I could see that making things even more dangerous. Eight health seems to be the player average, meaning five damage is when you start to see combat penalties, and eight is when your character is unconscious (and has eight minutes left until death). Two 10s suddenly turns from a quarter of a character's health pool and a moderate chance for more to half incapacitation.<br /> <br /> Maybe make automatic successes one of the options players can take for willpower expenditure?<br /> <br /> More likely, I'd just tell my players to stop being babies. Luck is the nature of the game. If it wasn't a factor, we'd just compare stat values. Sometimes the enemy pulls a hat trick. Sometimes you do. And most of the time, confirmation bias ensures you that the former outweighs the latter. Luckily, the new rules are designed to reward failure with experience. These games aren't about winning, they're about the highs and lows, and the more rare huge successes are, the more rewarding they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-25-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:50:42-07:00","id":976280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976188#post976188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping in mind probability is the same for NPCs and PCs, you should probably avoid using groups of NPCs as antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cant not use groups as i like humans as a threat to werewolves and the way Chrod has powercreep made it so that only in groups can &quot;regular&quot; people be a threat to werewolves even in dalu.<br /> <br /> That and the players decided to take on a gang head on. Maybe is there a rules for group of goons i missed? To be honest i read the WtF 2nd ed book but i really skimmed through the Chrod Blue book.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:58:03-07:00","id":976287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976280#post976280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I cant not use groups as i like humans as a threat to werewolves and the way Chrod has powercreep made it so that only in groups can &quot;regular&quot; people be a threat to werewolves even in dalu.<br /> <br /> That and the players decided to take on a gang head on. Maybe is there a rules for group of goons i missed? To be honest i read the WtF 2nd ed book but i really skimmed through the Chrod Blue book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The FFG Star Wars game uses a rule set for mobs that I think could work well in CoD. You put together a group of mooks that have significantly reduced stats that are pooled together, and the group only rolls once per turn. So maybe you have a group of three gangsters. They have 4 health a piece, a 2 dice attack roll, and each do 2 damage. That gives them 12 health as a group, roll 6 dice to attack, and 6 weapon damage when they're all alive. As soon as the players deal out 4 health, one of them is dead, and their weapon damage and attack roll is reduced to 4. Once another 4 damage is dealt, their damage and attack is reduced to 2. Scale accordingly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:00:14-07:00","id":976289,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976264#post976264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As nofather said, combat is the real point of contention. CoD combat is pretty damn deadly (particularly after the 2E rules changes), and I could see that making things even more dangerous. Eight health seems to be the player average, meaning five damage is when you start to see combat penalties, and eight is when your character is unconscious (and has eight minutes left until death). Two 10s suddenly turns from a quarter of a character's health pool and a moderate chance for more to half incapacitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will disgree there, in my experience so far 2nd edition had a power creep favoring too much for the side of supernaturals. Dalu forms applies defense agaisnt firearms and now defense is boosted making athletics the ones player mostly put most point into it with a average defense of 5 to 7. This without taking account gift etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976264#post976264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More likely, I'd just tell my players to stop being babies. Luck is the nature of the game. If it wasn't a factor, we'd just compare stat values. Sometimes the enemy pulls a hat trick. Sometimes you do. And most of the time, confirmation bias ensures you that the former outweighs the latter. Luckily, the new rules are designed to reward failure with experience. These games aren't about winning, they're about the highs and lows, and the more rare huge successes are, the more rewarding they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem for me at least on the DM side is i never know when a NPC i put is gonna &quot;nick&quot; the party or gonna obliterate them. I have been taking notes of all the rolls results so far and has being mostly all-or-nothing result. Either one side barely do anything or the dice keeps exploding until it seems chunky salsa.<br /> <br /> I mean there is a difference between &quot;sometimes enemies pull a trick&quot; and extreme failures and extreme destruction that seems to be ocurring, i dont blame the players they are a cool group and it not just them i notice that pattern too. Its one thing when a Big NPC can get lucky and another when a goon can murder a PC, i mean the PC should be &quot;scared&quot; and not know what could happen, i the DM however, shouldnt be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-25-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:06:40-07:00","id":976293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976287#post976287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The FFG Star Wars game uses a rule set for mobs that I think could work well in CoD. You put together a group of mooks that have significantly reduced stats that are pooled together, and the group only rolls once per turn. So maybe you have a group of three gangsters. They have 4 health a piece, a 2 dice attack roll, and each do 2 damage. That gives them 12 health as a group, roll 6 dice to attack, and 6 weapon damage when they're all alive. As soon as the players deal out 4 health, one of them is dead, and their weapon damage and attack roll is reduced to 4. Once another 4 damage is dealt, their damage and attack is reduced to 2. Scale accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it should be less health maybe 2 a piece. A storm tropper has 5 health, while a PC starts with 10 (mostly) before andding the brawn stat, meaning you need 2 stormtroppers to have a NPC group barely bellow a PC, that and they dont gain skill increment until the 3rd stormtropper so it has only attribute-only attack stat which mean it skill is bellow the barest minimum for a combat oriented pc (attribute 2 and combat skill 1)<br /> <br /> I mean it could work but it would need lot of math.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:10:20-07:00","id":976297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976289#post976289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I will disgree there, in my experience so far 2nd edition had a power creep favoring too much for the side of supernaturals. Dalu forms applies defense agaisnt firearms and now defense is boosted making athletics the ones player mostly put most point into it with a average defense of 5 to 7. This without taking account gift etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The problem for me at least on the DM side is i never know when a NPC i put is gonna &quot;nick&quot; the party or gonna obliterate them. I have been taking notes of all the rolls results so far and has being mostly all-or-nothing result. Either one side barely do anything or the dice keeps exploding until it seems chunky salsa.<br /> <br /> A 12 dice monster NPC just does 3 damage while a 3 dice (all of this after applying defense etc) goons hits for 8 damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, I may be out of my element here. I don't actually know the rules for werewolves, but I'd assume they're designed to be combat monsters. But ridiculously oversized dice pools are something I've had to accommodate in my Hunter game. I made the foolish decision of letting my players take tricks, so they have disproportionately sized pools to draw from. I definitely get where you're coming from. CoD's combat rules mean there's a very, VERY significant range in how much damage can be done, and the group rules I suggested above would only exacerbate that, probably. The problem is, the higher the dice pool, the higher the chance of rerolls (particularly if characters have 9/8/7 agains).<br /> <br /> Opponents who make good use of cover, work as a team, and employ spray fire could maybe help you level the playing field? The more you pare down the dice pools with penalties, the less variance you're going to have in damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-25-2016, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:13:32-07:00","id":976299,"title":"","content":"And yeah, those point values were just placeholders. You'd obviously have to balance it (and I don't have the mathematical acumen or the appropriate knowledge of WtF to do it justice). The advantage of mobs like that is that they're front-loaded for damage. So if you have a mob and a boss monster, the trick is which you attack first and when you redirect your attacks. Bosses have more versatility and are going to take longer to affect their core stats (via wound penalties), whereas mobs are glass cannons with greatly diminishing returns per damage taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:15:21-07:00","id":976303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976264#post976264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More likely, I'd just tell my players to stop being babies. Luck is the nature of the game. If it wasn't a factor, we'd just compare stat values.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because some people have a lower preference for randomness does not mean they want <i>no</i> randomness. Telling them they are &quot;babies&quot; is a pretty mean thing to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea would be that any ability that allows for exploding dice like 8-again, 9-again or 10-again would be replace with counting as 2 success trading the posibility of &quot;infinity rerolls&quot; for 2 sure successes when triggered. This would not apply to rote action rerolls. </div> </div> </div>A 10-again die has an EV of 1/3. Getting +2 on 10 has an EV of 0.4<br /> A 10&amp;9-again die has an EV of 0.3*(10/8) = 0.375. Getting +2 on 9 or 10 has an EV of 0.5<br /> A 10&amp;9&amp;8-again die has an EV of 0.3*(10/7) = 0.429. Getting +2 on 8 or 9 or 10 has an EV of 0.6<br /> <br /> Personally I'd do it as: if you were rolling a 10-again or 9-again, then you get one automatic success per three die you roll. If you were rolling a 8-again, then one auto success per 2.5 dice you roll (i.e. 2 auto successes if rolling five dice etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/210-siven","name":"Siven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:18:33-07:00","id":976306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Siven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976303#post976303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because some people have a lower preference for randomness does not mean they want <i>no</i> randomness. Telling them they are &quot;babies&quot; is a pretty mean thing to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that fun is the primary concern of the game, and I try hard to accommodate the needs of my players.<br /> <br /> But I also understand that these rules were built with balance in mind, and I'm very wary about upending the rules in a significant way just because there's some element of the game my players don't like.<br /> <br /> Besides, I play with people I love. Calling one another babies is pretty mild rapport in our day-to-day friendships. &quot;Deal with it&quot; is a pretty standard and necessary turn of phrase when you're playing with a group of varied and experienced players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:23:10-07:00","id":976312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976297#post976297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I may be out of my element here. I don't actually know the rules for werewolves, but I'd assume they're designed to be combat monsters. But ridiculously oversized dice pools are something I've had to accommodate in my Hunter game. I made the foolish decision of letting my players take tricks, so they have disproportionately sized pools to draw from. I definitely get where you're coming from. CoD's combat rules mean there's a very, VERY significant range in how much damage can be done, and the group rules I suggested above would only exacerbate that, probably. The problem is, the more successes, the higher the chance of rerolls (particularly if characters have 9/8/7 agains).</div> </div> </div> </div>But if the higher the dicerolls the more the chances of dicerolls wouldnt that mean that in the current rules a lets say, a 7 dicepool could net you lots of dice rolls maybe even 3 times while a with my suggestion a 7 dicepool at its most lucky would net you 14 successes? No matter the dice pool at most you would get double in success as a top. And even then 7 dicepool is a lot considering most defense range the 5 to 10.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976297#post976297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opponents who make good use of cover, work as a team, and employ spray fire could maybe help you level the playing field? The more you pare down the dice pools with penalties, the less variance you're going to have in damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been using cover, allout attack and burst for the goons that how they reach 4 dices instead chance die against dalu werewolf who apply their defense to firearms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-25-2016, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:27:02-07:00","id":976317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Siven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976303#post976303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'd do it as: if you were rolling a 10-again or 9-again, then you get one automatic success per three die you roll. If you were rolling a 8-again, then one auto success per 2.5 dice you roll (i.e. 2 auto successes if rolling five dice etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is interesting, specially because i have a full moon on the party which means they start the game with 8s again on combat rolls. My only problem with this is that except for the Full moon any ability that grants 9 again would be useless as everyone has the 10 again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:37:09-07:00","id":976324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976317#post976317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one is interesting, specially because i have a full moon on the party which means they start the game with 8s again on combat rolls. My only problem with this is that except for the Full moon any ability that grants 9 again would be useless as everyone has the 10 again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Option would be remove 10-again altogether. The difference between 10-again and non-exploding is small enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/210-siven","name":"Siven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:38:48-07:00","id":976325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Siven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976324#post976324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Option would be remove 10-again altogether. The difference between 10-again and non-exploding is small enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe try one session with one and then the other to see what my players preffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:44:47-07:00","id":976330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976312#post976312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But if the higher the dicerolls the more the chances of dicerolls wouldnt that mean that in the current rules a lets say, a 7 dicepool could net you lots of dice rolls maybe even 3 times while a with my suggestion a 7 dicepool at its most lucky would net you 14 successes? No matter the dice pool at most you would get double in success as a top. And even then 7 dicepool is a lot considering most defense range the 5 to 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the current system, a 1 str, 0 brawl character could hypothetically one punch murder another character to death on a chance roll. Granted, it 's a very, VERY rare chance, but it's there, if they keep hitting 10s over and over again, it's possible.<br /> <br /> The current rules vs. your proposed rules come down to this. Your rules have a higher chance of doing more damage on a regular basis. For every 10 dice a character rolls, one will be doubled. The existing rules have a lower chance of doing double damage and a very low (but not insurmountable) chance of doing more. For every 10 dice a character rolls, there's a one in three (approximate) chance another will be doubled), and a one in 10 chance that the character will have a three in ten chance of those dice being doubled. Rolling triple 10s though, at least in my experience, is pretty damn rare.<br /> <br /> From my perspective, it doesn't really address the problem. From the sound of things, your players are irritated that the NPCs are luckier than them. Are they going to be any happier when those NPCs do more damage because the opponents get more 10s and double up?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak[/QUOTE</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">True that could work, my only issue is that is gonna bog down the game and lots of micromanaging on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely not sure it's a feasible system. It would DEFINITELY require micromanagement. You'd probably want to come up with templates to deal with it. And admittedly, the more I think about it, the less it seems well suited to CoD rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:47:21-07:00","id":976333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Siven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/976176-using-automatic-successes-replacing-exploding-dices?p=976324#post976324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Option would be remove 10-again altogether. The difference between 10-again and non-exploding is small enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That seems like the most reasonable solution to me! Given the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:04:11-07:00","id":976377,"title":"","content":"If you're going to chance things, removing rerolls and turning 9-again into a +1, and 8-again into a +2 is a simple solution, and not going to mess with the math of the game too much.<br /> <br /> I am going to go back to something that I think hasn't been given a lot of focus in this (mostly since it's been about to-the-death combat).<br /> <br /> The goal of the CofD rules are that 1 success is all you need to achieve meaningful successes.<br /> <br /> This is one of the big underlying differences where the 10s are double rules in the WoD 20th games or Exalted matters. In the WoD, 1 success rolled doesn't mean you did anything, you need to generally rack up a large number of successes to get a significant result.<br /> <br /> In the CofD, any success past the first is supposed to be gravy.<br /> <br /> Obviously combat is a bit of a special situation because when fighting to the death, one success isn't usually going to end the fight. But in the end, the system doesn't need more successes generated per roll.<br /> <br /> And yes, the system favors supernaturals... because they're monsters that have the power to easily make normal human's lives miserable. Calling the 2e stuff &quot;power creep&quot; is a bit odd considering how much 1e fans were unhappy with how weak supernaturals were in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}